{"task": "Navigate to the page for the fifth alphabetical section identified. Extract a list of all the distinct "articles" (e.g., sets of rules like the Federal Rules of Evidence) contained within this section.

The fifth alphabetical section identified is: Federal Rules of Bankruptcy Procedure.
The main index page for Federal Rules is: https://www.law.cornell.edu/rules"}

{"function": "() => {
    // Find all list items that contain PART headings
    const parts = [];
    // The structure: each PART is a listitem with a text node containing the PART title
    // Then a nested list of rule items
    // We'll traverse the DOM
    const main = document.querySelector('main');
    if (!main) return [];
    // Find all list items within the article
    const listItems = main.querySelectorAll('li');
    let currentPart = null;
    let currentRules = [];
    for (let li of listItems) {
        const text = li.textContent.trim();
        // Check if text starts with "PART"
        if (text.startsWith('PART')) {
            // Save previous part
            if (currentPart) {
                parts.push({ part: currentPart, rules: currentRules });
            }
            currentPart = text;
            currentRules = [];
        } else if (text.startsWith('Rule') || text.startsWith('Rule ') || text.startsWith('Rule\u00A0')) {
            // Rule item
            currentRules.push(text);
        }
    }
    // Add last part
    if (currentPart) {
        parts.push({ part: currentPart, rules: currentRules });
    }
    return parts;
}"}

